yves salara was inspired by art the  french fashion designers creations often  mirrored his favorite artworks or echoed  their essence through colour or pattern  painters including brock and picasso  infused  creative vision he never copied but  reinvented in his unique style the  pompidou center is one of six top  museums in paris showcasing the  influence of art on the designer he was  picking up different kind of  inspirations from the contemporary  artists like warhol or wesselmann or  royensenstein but also modern artists  matisse or even pharmacology we could  say he had like a museum without walls  in his mind this pompidou curator says  the exhibition illustrates how fashion  can be an art form  it's an honor for us to have yves saint  laurent's creations alongside our  permanent collection in the pompidou and  i think it's the first time the show has  made a link between the designer's work  and contemporary art eve salary's love  affair with art is nowhere more evident  than in his mondrian inspired dresses a  tribute to the dutch artist daring  playful and modern they caused a  sensation when revealed in 1965.  as well as the pompidou center paris's  modern art museum the orsay picasso and  ysl museums are all part of the  exhibition but the most prestigious is  the louvre where some of sauron's most  luxurious and intricate designs reveal  his passion for ornamental art and all  things gold  i think the absolute dream for him would  have been to be exhibited for his  designs to interact with his sources of  inspiration  it's a dream he never imagined would  actually happen  [Music]  revolutionized women's fashion he gave  women beauty but also power he  challenged ideals and upset stereotypes  sixty years after his first fashion show  and more than a decade after his death  dozens of salahurang garments and 300  designs will be on show an enticing  tribute to one of the world's most  revered designers natasha butler al  jazeera paris
 

